      "math_academy_id": "e-4395",
      "problem": "Which of the following matrices are lower triangular matrices?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14251131/assets/7b0f54468ed1ed42c3f7b3d50779aa29c61df2a55a296151f8e262ce542b9673.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "The matrix $B$ is a lower triangular matrix since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $A$ and $C$ are *not* lower triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23} & =1\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{13} & =1\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
